# OpenCode: Modern Code Editor Setup on Termux (New Style)

This guide walks you through setting up a **modern, lightweight, open-source code editor** on Termux — we call this **OpenCode Style**. It gives you a full IDE experience (syntax highlighting, IntelliSense, Git integration, extensions) directly from your Android device's browser or terminal.

We'll use **code-server** (VS Code in the browser) as the primary method because it's fast, familiar, and works out-of-the-box on Termux.

---

## 📱 Prerequisites

- Android device with **Termux** installed (from [F-Droid](https://f-droid.org/en/packages/com.termux/) or GitHub – **not** the outdated Google Play version).
- At least **500 MB** free storage.
- Stable Wi-Fi (extensions may download additional assets).
- Basic familiarity with the terminal.

---

## 🚀 Step 1: Update Termux and Install Core Tools

Open Termux and run:

